<description>
Complete every same-colored frame with the union of that color's internal motif positions.

Input structure
The grid is a rectangular array of equal-size colored frames separated by background rows and columns.
Each frame has a solid one-pixel border and may contain additional pixels of its own color inside.

Rule
For each frame color, collect all relative positions occupied by that color across every frame of that
color, then repaint those positions into every frame with that color.

Key insight
Repeated frame colors are duplicate motif carriers: incomplete copies are completed by sharing the
relative colored-cell mask within the color group.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "transform_in_place",
  "src": "uniform colored frames separated by background, grouped by frame color",
  "transform": "for each color group, take the union of relative colored-pixel positions across its frames and paint that union into every frame of that color"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: R x C rows/cols where R = 1 + Nr*(5+1), C = 1 + Nc*(5+1); Nr 2-4, Nc 2-4 [observed]
  background: 0
  layout:
    frame_size: 5x5 (square, 1px solid border + 3x3 interior) [observed]
    gap: 1 row/col of bg between adjacent frames [observed]
    padding: 1 row/col of bg on all four grid edges [observed]
  frames:
    total: Nr * Nc (6-16)
    each_frame: single non-bg color; border is solid 1px of that color; interior cells are either that color or bg
    colors: 4-7 distinct non-bg colors, each assigned to 1-5 frames
    multi_frame_groups: 1-5 color groups with >=2 frames; at most 1 frame per group has interior motif pixels, rest are border-only
    single_frame_colors: 0-4 colors appearing once; may or may not have interior pixels
  motif:
    interior_size: 3x3 (frame_size - 2)
    filled_cells: 0-5 out of 9 interior positions per motif [observed]
    pattern: arbitrary (no symmetry required)
  transform:
    rule: for each color group, take union of interior motif across all frames of that color, paint into every frame
    effect: incomplete (border-only) frames of a multi-frame color receive the motif from the one frame that has it

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. pick Nr in [2,4], Nc in [2,4]; compute grid size = 1 + Nr*6 rows, 1 + Nc*6 cols
    2. pick K = Nr*Nc distinct non-bg colors; assign each frame cell (i,j) a color; ensure 1-5 groups have size >=2
    3. for each color, design one canonical 3x3 interior motif (0-5 filled cells); this is the OUTPUT state
    4. build output grid: place 5x5 frames at positions (1+i*6, 1+j*6) with solid border + canonical motif interior
    5. derive input: for each multi-frame color group with >=1 filled cell, keep motif in exactly 1 randomly chosen frame; clear interior (set to bg) in all other frames of that group
    6. single-frame colors keep their motif unchanged between input and output
